# iOS / Apple Code Signing — Best Practices

Applies to all release builds and CI. Signing is **manual** in CI; secrets never enter
the repo.

## Never commit / never hardcode

- No certificates (`.cer`, `.p12`), provisioning profiles (`.mobileprovision`,
  `.provisionprofile`), App Store Connect API keys (`.p8`), or passwords in the repo.
- `.gitignore` must cover `*.p12`, `*.mobileprovision`, `*.provisionprofile`, `*.p8`,
  `*.cer`, `AuthKey_*.p8`, exported `*.ipa`/`*.xcarchive`, and any keychain files.
- Secrets live in **Azure DevOps Secure Files** + secret pipeline variables / variable
  groups (ideally backed by Azure Key Vault).

## CI signing flow (Azure DevOps native)

1. `InstallAppleCertificate@2` — imports the `.p12` from Secure Files into a **temporary
   keychain** (password from a secret variable). Sets `$(APPLE_CERTIFICATE_SIGNING_IDENTITY)`.
2. `InstallAppleProvisioningProfile@1` — installs the profile; sets `$(APPLE_PROV_PROFILE_UUID)`.
3. `xcodebuild archive` / `-exportArchive` with `CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual`,
   `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM`, and `PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER` from those variables.
4. **App Store Connect API key** (Issuer ID + Key ID + base64 `.p8`) for TestFlight /
   App Store uploads via `AppStoreRelease@1`. Prefer API key over Apple ID + app-specific
   password (no 2FA prompts, revocable, scoped).

## Signing style

- **Local archive/export:** default **Automatic** — provisioning profiles and team come from
  the **`.xcodeproj` / `.pbxproj`** and the Xcode account (`-allowProvisioningUpdates`).
  Use skills **`xc-archive`** and **`xc-export`**; do not override profiles unless asked.
- **CI release/archive:** **Manual** signing with `InstallAppleCertificate@2` +
  `InstallAppleProvisioningProfile@1` (reproducible). Pass `-SigningStyle Manual` to
  `xc-archive`.
- One distribution certificate (**Apple Distribution**) per team; rotate before expiry.
- Match the export method to the profile: `development`, `ad-hoc`, `app-store-connect`,
  `enterprise`, `developer-id`, `mac-application`.

## Self-hosted Mac agents

- Use a **dedicated keychain per CI role**; unlock it in the pipeline before `xcodebuild`
  (`security unlock-keychain`) and add it to the search list (`security list-keychains -s`).
- Keep the login keychain uncluttered; clean up imported profiles/keychains after the run.
- Treat the `.p12` private key as KMS-grade: transfer only via Secure Files / encrypted
  channels. Enterprise certificate misuse can revoke an entire catalog — isolate strictly.

## Entitlements & capabilities

- Keep `*.entitlements` in source control (no secrets there). Capabilities must match the
  provisioning profile; mismatches fail export.
